# AGENTS.md: {{ service_name }}

{{ description }}. Part of **FamilyMeal**, a family meal planner: an LLM builds a 3–7 day
batch-cooking menu from a recipe catalog, recipes are imported by URL, and a shopping list
is built from the accepted plan.

This file is for coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, ...) and humans alike.
Cross-service rules, contracts and ADRs live in the **meal-platform** repository;
read its `AGENTS.md` before changing anything that crosses a service boundary.

## Commands

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Install deps and hooks | `make install` |
| Everything CI runs | `make check` |
| Lint / autofix | `make lint` / `make fmt` |
| Types (pyright strict) | `make typecheck` |
| Layer contracts (import-linter) | `make imports` |
| Tests | `make test` or `uv run pytest tests/test_x.py -k name` |
| Run locally | `cp .env.example .env && make run` → http://localhost:{{ http_port }}/docs |
| Pull template updates | `make update-template` |

Always run `make check` before saying a task is done. Never add a dependency with pip;
use `uv add <pkg>` (or `uv add --dev`) so `uv.lock` stays the source of truth.

## Layout and layering

```
src/{{ package_name }}/
  domain/          entities, value objects, domain errors, ports (typing.Protocol)
  application/     use cases: one module per use case, depends on domain only
  infrastructure/  adapters implementing ports: DB, Redis Streams, HTTP clients, LLM
  api/             FastAPI routers and request/response schemas
  observability/   logging, tracing, metrics, trace propagation (do not bypass)
  settings.py      pydantic-settings, env vars only
  main.py          composition root: create_app() wires everything together
tests/             mirrors src/; unit tests for domain/application, API tests via TestClient
```

Dependency direction: `api → application → domain ← infrastructure`.

- `domain` imports nothing from FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, httpx2, Redis, Ollama, `observability`
  or `settings`.
- `application` talks to the outside world only through ports defined in `domain`.
- Wiring (which adapter implements which port) happens in `main.py` / FastAPI dependencies.
- The LLM is just another port (`domain`) with an Ollama adapter (`infrastructure`).
  LLM output is always parsed into a Pydantic model; never pass raw LLM text into the domain.

## Code style

- Python {{ python_version }}, full type hints, pyright strict must pass. No `Any` in signatures
  of domain or application code; no `# type: ignore` without an error code and a reason.
- Pydantic models at the boundaries (API, events, LLM output, settings);
  plain dataclasses (frozen) inside the domain are fine.
- Async all the way for I/O. No blocking calls (`requests`, `time.sleep`) in async code.
- Small functions, explicit names, no clever metaprogramming. Comments explain *why*.
- Errors: domain raises domain exceptions; `api` maps them to HTTP status codes.

## Observability (non-negotiable)

Quality of logs, traces and metrics is a primary goal of this project.

- Logging: `from {{ package_name }}.observability import get_logger`;
  `logger = get_logger(__name__)`. Never `print`, never `logging.getLogger` (ruff bans it).
- Log events are dotted snake_case names with key-value context, not prose:
  `logger.info("recipe.imported", recipe_id=..., source="json-ld")`. No f-strings in messages.
- Never log secrets, tokens or full LLM prompts with personal data.
- Incoming HTTP and outgoing httpx2 calls are traced automatically. Add a manual span for every
  use case and every LLM call: `with get_tracer(__name__).start_as_current_span("plan.generate"):`.
  Put useful ids on spans as attributes (`span.set_attribute("recipe.id", ...)`).
- Events between services: producers add `inject_trace_context()` to the message fields;
  consumers start a `SpanKind.CONSUMER` span with `context=extract_trace_context(fields)`.
  One user action must be one trace across all services.
- Business metrics through `get_meter(__name__)` (counters/histograms), names like
  `recipes.imported`, with low-cardinality attributes only.

## Testing

- pytest, `asyncio_mode = auto`. Arrange / act / assert, one behavior per test.
- Domain and application: fast unit tests with fakes for ports, no network.
- API: `TestClient` via the `client` fixture. Observability can be asserted with the
  `span_exporter` and `log_exporter` fixtures (see `tests/test_observability.py`).
- Warnings are errors in tests. Fix the cause instead of filtering it.
- Every bug fix starts with a failing test.

## Contracts

- HTTP API: FastAPI generates OpenAPI; the copy in meal-platform `contracts/openapi/` is
  updated in the same change when the API changes.
- Events: schemas in meal-platform `contracts/events/`. Add fields, never rename or remove
  them without a new event version.

## Boundaries for agents

- Ask before: adding a new runtime dependency, changing a contract, changing CI or Dockerfile,
  touching anything in `observability/` beyond adding helpers.
- Never: commit secrets or `.env`, disable or skip tests to get green, weaken pyright or ruff
  settings, edit `.copier-answers.yml` by hand.
- Files that come from meal-service-template (CI, Dockerfile, observability, tooling config)
  should be improved in the template and pulled with `make update-template`.

